<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Derive the quadratic formula — fill in the missing steps</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Work through the derivation of the quadratic formula from \(a x^2 + b x + c = 0\) (with \(a \neq 0\)) by completing the square. Fill in each missing step. Give <strong>exact</strong> expressions in terms of \(a\), \(b\) and \(c\) (no decimals).</p>
<p>Dividing every term by \(a\) gives \[ x^2 + \frac{b}{a}x + \frac{c}{a} = 0. \]</p>

<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> Move the constant term to the right-hand side.</p>
<div>\( x^2 + \frac{b}{a}x = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><strong>Step 2.</strong> To complete the square, what single term must be added to <em>both</em> sides?</p>
<div>Add \(\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> The left-hand side is now \(\left(x+\frac{b}{2a}\right)^2\). Write the right-hand side as a single fraction over \(4a^2\).</p>
<div>\( \left(x+\frac{b}{2a}\right)^2 = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>

<p><strong>Step 4.</strong> Take square roots and solve for \(x\). Give the two solutions as a set, e.g. \(\{\,\alpha,\ \beta\,\}\).</p>
<div>\( x \in \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Completing the square on the general equation gives the quadratic formula:</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
a x^2 + b x + c &= 0\\
x^2 + \tfrac{b}{a}x + \tfrac{c}{a} &= 0 &&\text{(divide by } a\text{)}\\
x^2 + \tfrac{b}{a}x &= -\tfrac{c}{a} &&\textbf{(Step 1)}\\
x^2 + \tfrac{b}{a}x + \left(\tfrac{b}{2a}\right)^2 &= -\tfrac{c}{a} + \tfrac{b^2}{4a^2} &&\textbf{(Step 2: add } \tfrac{b^2}{4a^2}\text{)}\\
\left(x+\tfrac{b}{2a}\right)^2 &= \tfrac{b^2-4ac}{4a^2} &&\textbf{(Step 3)}\\
x + \tfrac{b}{2a} &= \pm\tfrac{\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\
x &= \dfrac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a} &&\textbf{(Step 4)}
\end{align*}
\]
<p>The two solutions are \(\left\{\dfrac{-b-\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a},\ \dfrac{-b+\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\right\}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
